{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2e9fb001e4bae91c4a1af297fc7af1bcd469f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(ab+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157b1248bad25e9621cdf712aa24411ec4698a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are Fibonacci numbers.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72b836a2d3e487aa36f1e6c63fc952fefd4dfe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Note$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />: Euler’s totient function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d7e990c9ebf7adc93ddd233b1239e5e4c0eef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of positive integers less than\nor equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2JELC4OEO0A\">https://youtu.be/2JELC4OEO0A</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c1914c3c86cc102dd4e5a279c481daeec3e8e9df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4fb304e527f209c084535d11971b5495e46153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid \\varphi (ab+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de1b98ef17117d4d8f629af51fc9992d1282590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid a^2+b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" />, so one is even and the other is odd. \n</p><p>This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/8253b492e096f2b3c330fff33ad7bc50a43a0efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+1\\equiv 2\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/332950e9f3fac7928c161ea090f7df5559d3ad76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu _2 (\\varphi(ab+1))=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />. To use this, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdd1b6020d06e128ebbf864c96f69863d687dd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is odd.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65a3c460e4801b769daf521423dadb282ef87ed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1 = p_1^{e_1}p_2^{e_2}\\dots p_n^{e_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa82c42b33ae8ebe0fd76a2cebb526348b3d32b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1, p_2, \\dots, p_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" /> are odd primes. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deab1c875424552a2ee473ae6ae61ad708cc4f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\nu _2 (\\varphi (ab+1)) = \\nu _2 \\left (\\ \\prod_{i=1}^{n} p_i^{e_i-1}(p_i-1) \\right ) \\geq n\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"53\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80ece6157790bfadf3ab558dc4d9f79254146f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1 = p^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" /> for some odd prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Furthermore, by the above reasoning, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3caf39337895e4513decdd3399e7284b4e8acf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a0ef476cf5452cdb5a980c9697dc1068e0731b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /></b>\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f294a58cc4762402465aa9b0097757cec749883a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\nmid a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/9002c726e1876d3b17280b8b374ddf8cc516a4ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab+1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{p^{k-1}}\\implies b\\equiv -a^{-1} \\pmod{p^{k-1}}\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"20\" /> Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6c6c1b3c2ca449ad246f8dbbb3986a91e4a5df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{k-1} \\mid \\varphi (ab+1) \\mid a^2+b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"22\" />, so we can substitute like so:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9041943e8f524214cd32b044f2667d04b41ebf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2+1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{p^{k-1}} \\implies a^2+\\frac{1}{a^2}+1\\equiv 0 \\pmod{p^{k-1}}\\]\" width=\"506\" height=\"37\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf5c4b0f7714f143be142b4de94ed8c349a2db9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 4a^4+4a^2+4 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{p^{k-1}} \\implies (2a^2+1)^2 \\equiv -3 \\pmod{p^{k-1}}\\implies \\left(\\frac{-3}{p}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"679\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4dbd6ad996cd00a817ea92c848b273c324c8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"36\" height=\"43\" /> is the Legendre symbol. By quadratic reprocity, using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/839a519971a80950aa6be09553d6b4b238aa6ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c75f13b9c10bde6550d91d110e8a1d0ecdbdb20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{-3}{p}\\right) =\\left(\\frac{3}{p}\\right) \\left(\\frac{-1}{p}\\right) = -\\left(\\frac{3}{p}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{p}{3}\\right)\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"43\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a334775104592618fcf98fefb6476b943eaf29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{p}{3}\\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"35\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6ca8286e53610980b4c352babc815a3f10d501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}\\implies p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417c8a5ce1328bf1331251ee78aab9ba331e80bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n<b>Subcase 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /></b>\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd08697555128b0a37db02287b4de72e6cb4b463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-3}{9}\\right) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"103\" height=\"45\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/186443498b315b2c525bb57db0f9a3b226fe7c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1\\leq 1\\implies k=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"169\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982d005a81b1e7837ef64828e4abab652fa39c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. It easy to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f712acca97a9edee78368cc7d21842c871addb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (1, 8), (8, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> are the only solutions in this case. Since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are Fibonacci numbers, this subcase is complete.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Subcase 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417c8a5ce1328bf1331251ee78aab9ba331e80bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /></b> \n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3600fdbc63011823cd9dea094871856d59d468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\mid p-1 \\mid \\varphi (ab+1) \\mid a^2+b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"257\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cfc8529e9df21fca1903896210d62ff4387bc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\nmid a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/491b103044963c6a9e53b579a98dcf9c65d2604f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1 \\equiv p^k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\implies 3 \\mid ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"289\" height=\"22\" />, a contradiction. Thus, this subcase yields no solutions.\n</p><p>Putting all of the above together completes the first case.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><b>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /></b>\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73fd38433e59ee42b6f59b6d975a95c434f84193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+1=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114a64fc9aaf1dfc4bcbd7b7a88eafb5a4134087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(ab+1)=ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />, and the problem condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15bfbe91a16c22c28c6c2683253675e01a4fa0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\mid a^2+b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442bd799c96fe04bd214501382be6bc7e8a2a2fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2+b^2+1}{ab}=t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is a positive integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be the pair with the minimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d997b30f7f09d32954c9b09f04a6599729dd6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c7aaf080a92e9c019d23e0530d9410c58e91ca8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2-tab+b^2+1=0\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" /> We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is one of the roots of this quadratic. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the other root of this quadratic. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf25a72eea1c5b6a88d635611bf761bf8ac15ab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = tb-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b53faed839dda51e9fc2812ef5557afaa002be4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{b^2+1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" />. The first equation proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, and the second proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive. Furthermore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5591a62c2967435bdb34c69dd64009580096fc61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2+1 &lt;a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22bd364983006cb2c46a3f7fc682836d1ade446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{b^2+1}{a} &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"41\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb635bb9096d9f3dbb1566f4e3475f58569d8f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> as a valid pair, a contradiction. Thus, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> for this minimal pair. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51045abc73cea2e7d831d6140f4f0437ad1ec60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 \\mid 2a^2+1 \\implies a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a703cc5d184428a3abb234b4238ebc6cf97de3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b) = (1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c913cff7776ae19bed793a777bfc7157591527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, since otherwise we could follow the above logic to obtain a contradiction by infinite descent.\n</p><p><br />\nWe claim that all solutions are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f302314274d2de3e2ad2a1f49afb2a18071a09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b) = (F_i, F_{i-2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b720b9f3685aab02e5347b185fd6a680c87ded5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(F_{i-2}, F_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />. Proceed by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of solutions such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d616ac4b402d61fdfad18863282c6ea697f5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\leq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. For the base case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a192c0837252285a8e001d5d07004f3aaaa5e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k = \\{(1, 1)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. Now, assume that all solutions in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/725637ad7ac13e69f84fbad6d938b2ceb962aba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{k-1}, k\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> are Fibonacci numbers. \n</p><p>Suppose we have a solution such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e7413cac0998ec739a96de293f1bb5c57cbe7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d997b30f7f09d32954c9b09f04a6599729dd6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. By the above logic, we have a smaller <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b8a746afa435a574d2153f0a8cc6f5dd4e4d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3b - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b53faed839dda51e9fc2812ef5557afaa002be4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{b^2+1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff258ccdd14498ab730507a5cf8d5d10c33626d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cccaff7eb08233edea3022ea546944c1944423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{b^2+1}{a} &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"41\" />. Furthermore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c5c2151041431935f5bfdacbd23c7bca6c88c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b, x)\\in S_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c2de017922e4d07c865c2cc26226c7e46f74a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = F_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/7337addf6dc18856f63ca9cfd84308c8df47ca76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = F_{i-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaac17c82376648ae45b25a8a015bbefa3f33541.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 3b-x = 3F_i - F_{i-2} = 2F_i + F_{i-1} = F_{i+1}+F_i = F_{i+2}\\]\" width=\"450\" height=\"17\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae99d0294cfe9c6a459c72ff342888068f00046f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b) = (F_{i+2}, F_{i})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. This completes the induction. \n</p><p><br />\nPutting all this together finishes the second case. Finally, the proof is complete <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~Dedekind cuts for idea (video solution)\n</p><p>~sillybone\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018035247\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 497/1000000\nPost‐expand include